<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27321" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lycāŏnes</span></b> ,
		um, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λυκάονες</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the Lycaonians, a people of Asia Minor, between
				Cappadocia, Cilicia, and Pisidia</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 2,
			5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 29, 29, §
			105</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lycāŏnĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>adj., Lycaonian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lycaoniumque Ericeten,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 10, 749</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lycāŏnia</span></b> ,
			ae, f., <i>the country of the
				Lycaonians</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Att. 5, 15, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 37,
				54, 11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">38,
			39</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Act. 14, 6</span></i>.—Hence,
				adv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lycāŏnĭcē</span></b> ,
				<i>in the dialect of Lycaonia</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dicentes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Act. 14, 10</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
